    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="1100" n="994" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg994"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) City of Flint/42: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-27T10:00:00+03:00">October 27,
                            1939—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 27—6:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>810. My 809, October 27, 5 a.m. I was unable to obtain the promised telephone
                    communication with the Captain or a member of the crew of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of Flint</hi> at 8 this morning, although temporary
                    communication with the Murmansk operator was established. As calls for Murmansk
                    are only accepted for certain hours during the day the next attempt will be made
                    at 1:30 today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
